1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,800
(Howard:)So two years later,
there's a knock on the door.

2
00:00:05,964 --> 00:00:07,844
Guy opens it, and there is the snail...

3
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:10,928
(Howard:)...who says,
"What the heck was all that about?"

4
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:13,054
[CHUCKLES]

5
00:00:13,388 --> 00:00:15,218
(Bernadette:)I don't really get it.

6
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:20,022
(Howard:)Well, see, it took two years
for the snail to--

7
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:24,897
(Howard:)Not important.

8
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:27,613
(Bernadette:)-Can I ask you a question?
-Sure.

9
00:00:27,777 --> 00:00:30,367
(Bernadette:)Where do you think this is going?

10
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,701
(Howard:)To be honest,
I was hoping at least second base.

11
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:36,702
(Bernadette:)You're so funny.

12
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:40,377
(Bernadette:)You're like a standup comedian.

13
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:44,210
(Howard:)A Jewish standup comedian,
that would be new.

14
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:48,465
(Bernadette:)Actually, I think a lot of them
are Jewish.

15
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:52,385
No, I was just-- Because-- Never mind.

16
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:57,311
(Bernadette:)Look, Howard, this is our third date,
and we both know what that means.

17
00:00:57,474 --> 00:01:00,064
(Howard:)-We do?
-Sex.

18
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,394
(Howard:)You're kidding.

19
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:08,236
(Bernadette:)But I need to know whether
you're looking for a relationship...

20
00:01:08,401 --> 00:01:09,981
(Bernadette:)...or a one-night stand.

21
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:13,944
(Howard:)Okay, just to be clear,
there's only one correct answer, right?

22
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,619
I mean, it's not like "Chicken or fish?"
on an airplane?

23
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:19,916
(Bernadette:)Maybe you need to think about it
a little.

24
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,910
Well, you know, it's not unheard of...

25
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,922
(Howard:)...for a one-night stand
to turn into a relationship.

26
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:30,251
(Bernadette:)Call me when you figure it out.

27
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:36,926
(Howard:)Three dates means sex?

28
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,728
(Howard:)Who knew?

29
00:01:43,853 --> 00:01:45,023
[TV PLAYING]

30
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:47,228
Greetings, homeys.

31
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:49,152
(Howard:)Homette.

32
00:01:49,734 --> 00:01:51,694
(Penny:)Why are you back from your date
so early?

33
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:57,531
Well, in romance, as in show business,
always leave them wanting more.

34
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:03,043
(Penny:)-What exactly does that mean?
-He struck out.

